    "https://uottawa.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uOttawa_External_Career_Site/job/Ottawa-ON/APTPUO---BMG5109-C---Winter-2027_JR39613-1": {
      "title": "APTPUO - BMG5109 C - Winter 2027",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nPart time\n\nPosting Reason: New Position Location: Main Campus Academic Period: 2027 Winter Semester Faculty: Faculté de génie / Faculty of Engineering Academic Unit: Département de génie mécanique \\\\ Department of Mechanical Engineering Course Title: Advanced Topics in Medical Instrumentation Course Code: BMG5109 Section: C Course Description: Specialized theoretical and practical approach to the design and implementation of systems related to medical diagnosis. The design process includes the integration of state of the art tools and technologies to acquire, analyze and process vital medical signals. Translating theory into industrial medical diagnostic products and services. Introduction to artificial intelligence and its applications to problems of medical diagnosis. Engineering technologies (biosensors, diagnostic imaging, lab tests, etc) and medical diagnostic process (signs and symptoms) will be integrated and combined in one engineering process to create intelligent and fully automated medical diagnostic systems. Posting limited to: Professeur à temps-partiel régulier / Regular Part-Time Professor Date Posted (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/10/02 Applications must be received BEFORE (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/11/02 Expected Enrolment: 25 Approval date: 2026/10/02 Number of credits: 3 Work Hours: 39 Hourly Rate: Enseignement / Teaching: $239.47 (2024-2025) The academic year starts on September 1 and ends on August 31. These rates do not included vacation pay nor statutory pay. These rates will be applied until a new collective agreement is ratified. Retro will be paid after the ratification. Course type: C Posting type: Régulier / Regular Language of instruction: Anglais | English Competence in second language: Passive Course Schedule: Jeudi | Thursday 19:00-22:00 - - Requirements: Candidate profile: PhD in Biomedical, Mechanical or Electrical Engineering or related discipline with specialization, Strong background and demonstrate expe