    "https://uottawa.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uOttawa_External_Career_Site/job/Ottawa-ON/English-language-replacement-professor-position--at-the-rank-of-Assistant-Professor_JR39403": {
      "title": "English-language replacement professor position, at the rank of Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nPosting Reason: New Position Job Family: Academic Leadership and Faculty Union affiliation: APUO Faculty/Department: Faculty of Education_FT Campus: Main Campus Date Posted (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/10/02 Applications must be received BEFORE (YYYY/MM/DD): The Faculty of Education at the University of Ottawa invites applications for one English-language replacement professor position, at the rank of Assistant Professor. Area of teaching and research: second language education.   The Faculty of Education at the University of Ottawa is located on the ancestral territories of the Algonquin people, in the heart of the nation’s capital. With more than fifty professors, it offers an exceptional intellectual environment for its students, researchers and professors. Open to the world, the Faculty is committed to providing students with a rich and stimulating experience and to promoting excellence in research. This recruitment reflects the current Faculty of Education’s strategic plan, which emphasizes social and ecological justice, well-being, and excellence and innovation in teaching and research.   Overall duties: The overall duties of the position include, in varying proportions: a) teaching activities; b) scholarly activities demonstrated through research, literary or artistic creation, or professional activities; and c) activities related to service to the university community. The specific duties for this position are associated with directing the Professional Development Program (PDP), and the coordination of the Teacher training in technology education (Edutek). Collaboration with the Francophone and Anglophone sectors of the Faculty is an important dimension of the position.   Term: New replacement position for a 2-year contract, from January 1st, 2027, to June 30th, 2028.   Salary: The salary scale for an Assistant Professor begins at $99,377 (as of May 1, 2025).   Benefits: The University of Ottawa provides a comprehensive benefits package including long-term disability insurance, basic life insurance, supplementary health insurance, the University of Ottawa pension plan, and optional life insurance.   Location of work: Faculty of Education, University of Ottawa, Lamoureux Hall, 145 Jean-Jacques-Lussier Private, Ottawa, Ontario, K1N 6N5.   Contact information: Dr. Mirela Moldoveanu, Ph.D., Vice-Dean, Undergraduate Programs, Faculty of Education, University of Ottawa, Email: vdgouv@uOttawa.ca . Telephone: 613-562-5800, ext. 4062.   Requirements: Education: Ph.D. in Education or equivalent in a field related to the position Work experience: Excellent program management skills. Demonstrated ability to teach at the undergraduate and graduate levels in an interdisciplinary collaborative context. Candidates must also demonstrate the skills and openness needed to deliver courses in hybrid and online formats. Teaching and research experience in second language didactics. Assets: skills in entrepreneurship, pedagogical innovation, and partnership development. Passive knowledge of English is essential. Full French-English bilingualism is considered essential. Applications should include: an up-to-date curriculum vitae, a cover letter outlining your achievements in program management as well as your teaching and research interests, a sample of scholarly work, the names and contact information of three referees, and a transcript for each university degree received. Your application should be addressed to: Mirela Moldoveanu, Ph.D. Vice-Dean, Undergraduate programs Faculty of Education University of Ottawa vdgouv @uOttawa.ca Telephone: 613-562-5800, ext. 4062   The selection process will begin on November 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. However, only shortlisted candidates will be contacted.   More information regarding Academic Careers can be found online . Apply online through the University of Ottawa Careers portal. The University of Ottawa is committed to ensuring equity, diversity, and inclusion in the scholarly and leadership environments of our students, staff, and faculty. Accordingly, we strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples in Canada, visible minorities members (racialized persons), persons with disabilities, women, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with equitable, diverse, and inclusive communities. Candidates who wish to be considered as a member of one or more designated groups are asked to complete the confidential Self-Identification Questionnaire, to be completed at the time of application.   All qualified candidates are invited to apply; however, preference will be given to Canadians and permanent residents. When submitting your application, please indicate if you are legally entitled to work in Canada   The University of Ottawa provides accommodations for applicants with disabilities throughout the recruitment process. If you are invited to proceed in the selection process, please notify us of any accommodations that you require by contacting the Office of the Vice-Provost, Faculty Relations by email at vra.affairesprofessorales@uottawa.ca . Any information you send us will be handled respectfully and in complete confidence.   The University of Ottawa is proud of its 160-year tradition of bilingualism. Through its Official Languages and Bilingualism Institute, the University provides training to staff members and to their spouses in their second official language.   Prior to May 1, 2022, the University required all students, faculty, staff, and visitors (including contractors) to be fully vaccinated against Covid-19 as defined in Policy 129 – Covid-19 Vaccination. This policy was suspended effective May 1, 2022 but may be reinstated at any point in the future depending on public health guidelines and the recommendations of experts."
    },
    "https://uottawa.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uOttawa_External_Career_Site/job/Ottawa-ON/Cupe-CORR-W27-MAT-1730c-30h_JR39785": {
      "title": "Cupe_CORR_W27_MAT-1730c_30h",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nPart time\n\nPosting Reason: New Position Location where work is to be performed: STEM Session: 2027 Winter Semester | Trimestre d'hiver Faculty: Faculté des sciences / Faculty of Science Unit: Department of Mathematics and Statistics, Students & Casuals Job Classification: Corrector (CUPE) Posting Type: Cours précis / Specific course Course Title: Calcul différentiel et intégral pour les sciences de la vie I Course Code: MAT-1730 Section: C Supervisor name (if known): Date Posted (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/10/05 Applications must be received BEFORE (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/10/31 Description of tasks (hours): Unless specified below, specific allocation of hours to various tasks should be articulated in a description of work negotiated and signed by you and the supervising professor prior to the commencement of work. Recherche / Research:0 Préparation / Preparation:0 Contact avec étudiants / Contact with Students:0 Correction - Notation / Grading:30 Surveillance / Proctoring:0 Formation / Training:0 Autre / Other:0 Number of positions: 2 Expected Enrolment: 95 Work Start Date: January 01, 2027 Work End Date: April 30, 2027 Total Work Hours: 30 Hourly Rate: Correcteur / Corrector : $31.44 ou/or $37.73 (Sept. 2025 - Aug. 2026) Undergraduate students will be paid at the lower rate; while graduate students will be paid at the higher rate. These rates do not include vacation pay nor statutory pay. Method of Delivery: En Personne Language of Work: Français | French Requirements and Nature of Work: Étudiant(e) ayant un minimum de 30 crédits en mathématiques & statistiques avec une bonne compréhension de la matière pour effectuer: • CORRECTION des examens de mi-session, des tests et d’autres travaux.   La priorité sera accordée aux étudiants-es des cycles supérieurs du département de mathématiques et de statistiques. Additional Information and/or Comments: All University of Ottawa employees are required under provincial law to successfully complete all mandatory legislated training offered by the University. The list of training requirements may be modified by provincial law. If you are invited to continue the selection process, please notify us of any particular adaptive measures you might require. We may consult with the Health and Wellness sector of Human Resources, if needed. Any information you send us will be handled respectfully and in complete confidence. The hiring process will be governed by the current CUPE 2626 collective agreement; you can click here to find out more. The University of Ottawa embraces diversity and inclusion in the workplace. We are passionate about our people and committed to employment equity. We foster a culture of respect, teamwork and inclusion, where collaboration, innovation, and creativity fuel our quest for research and teaching excellence. While all qualified persons are invited to apply, we welcome applications from qualified Indigenous persons, racialized persons, persons with disabilities, women and LGBTQIA2S+ persons. The University is committed to creating and maintaining an accessible, barrier-free work environment. The University is also committed to working with applicants with disabilities requesting accommodation during the recruitment, assessment and selection processes. Applicants with disabilities may contact the academic unit to communicate the accommodation need. Prior to May 1, 2022, the University required all students, faculty, staff, and visitors (including contractors) to be fully vaccinated against Covid-19 as defined in Policy 129 – Covid-19 Vaccination. This policy was suspended effective May 1, 2022 but may be reinstated at any point in the future depending on public health guidelines and the recommendations of experts."
