      "title": "CUPE - Winter2027 - TA DGD 65H - CHM2754",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nPart time\n\nPosting Reason: New Position Location where work is to be performed: Main Campus Session: 2027 Winter Semester | Trimestre d'hiver Faculty: Faculté des sciences / Faculty of Science Unit: Department of Chemistry and Biomolecular Sciences, Students & Casuals Job Classification: Teaching Assistant/Demonstrator/Lab Monitor (CUPE) Posting Type: Cours précis / Specific course Course Title: Chimie analytique Course Code: CHM 2754 Section: A00 Supervisor name (if known): Heshel Teitelbaum Date Posted (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/10/26 Applications must be received BEFORE (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/10/30 Description of tasks (hours): Unless specified below, specific allocation of hours to various tasks should be articulated in a description of work negotiated and signed by you and the supervising professor prior to the commencement of work. Recherche / Research:0 Préparation / Preparation:18 Contact avec étudiants / Contact with Students:18 Correction - Notation / Grading:23 Surveillance / Proctoring:6 Formation / Training:0 Autre / Other:0 Number of positions: 6 Expected Enrolment: 80 Work Start Date: January 01, 2027 Work End Date: April 30, 2027 Total Work Hours: 65 Hourly Rate: AE-RA-Tuteur / TA-RA-Tutor : $31.89 ou/or $50.25 (2024-2025) Undergraduate students will be paid at the lower rate; while graduate students will be paid at the higher rate. These rates do not include vacation pay nor statutory pay. Method of Delivery: In person Language of Work: Français | French Requirements and Nature of Work: Nature of Work Deliver and prepare DGD sessions. Supervise quizzes, midterms, and the final examination. Minimum Qualifications The candidate must have successfully completed one year of general chemistry, one year of organic chemistry, CHM 4354 , or their equivalents. Any individual who is not a graduate (Master’s or PhD) student in Chemistry must pass a qualifying test (unless previously completed). Additional Information and/or Comm