      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nPart time\n\nPosting Reason: New Position Location where work is to be performed: Main Campus Session: 2027 Winter Semester | Trimestre d'hiver Faculty: Faculté des sciences sociales / Faculty of Social Sciences Unit: School of International Development and Global Studies_ST Job Classification: Research Assistant (CUPE) Posting Type: Recherche / Research Course Title: RA in DVM (Prof. Gibb) Course Code: RA in DVM (Prof. Gibb) Section: Supervisor name (if known): Prof. Christine Gibb Date Posted (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/10/26 Applications must be received BEFORE (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/11/27 Description of tasks (hours): Unless specified below, specific allocation of hours to various tasks should be articulated in a description of work negotiated and signed by you and the supervising professor prior to the commencement of work. Recherche / Research:0 Préparation / Preparation:0 Contact avec étudiants / Contact with Students:0 Correction - Notation / Grading:0 Surveillance / Proctoring:0 Formation / Training:0 Autre / Other:0 Number of positions: 1 Expected Enrolment: 0 Work Start Date: janvier 01, 2027 Work End Date: avril 30, 2027 Total Work Hours: 117 Hourly Rate: AE-RA-Tuteur / TA-RA-Tutor : $33.83 ou/or $53.31 (Sept. 2026 - Aug. 2027) Undergraduate students will be paid at the lower rate; while graduate students will be paid at the higher rate. These rates do not include vacation pay nor statutory pay. Method of Delivery: in person Language of Work: Anglais | English Requirements and Nature of Work: Creation of disability and development pedagogical materials. The RA will develop teaching materials for a disability and development module in DVM 1100 (1-2 lectures and 1 DGD with lesson plan, teaching notes, slides, readings, supporting material for students plus 1 assignment and suggested exam questions) and for a disability and research module in DVM 3150 (1 lecture with lesson plan, teaching notes, slides, readings, supporting mate